PEAP Explained
PEAP = Protected EAP.

In your story: Allen's password is in a locked box before he hands it over. Nobody can read the password in transit.

How it works (simplified):

Mutley and the manager first set up a secure tunnel (TLS encryption) between them. No password involved yet — just the tunnel.
Once the tunnel is up, Allen's password travels inside that tunnel.
The manager checks the password. Done.
Why it exists: Without PEAP, Allen's password would be flying around in the open. PEAP wraps it in encryption first, so even if someone sniffs the wire, 
they see garbage.
